{{Quote|Have they been through here?|The tech stormtrooper, interrogating an alien|audio=TechStormtrooper-TheChildrenFromTehar.mp3|<ref name="The Children from Tehar" />}}
A [[human]] [[Gender|male]] served as a '''tech stormtrooper''' of the [[First Order]]. In [[34 ABY]], the [[tech stormtrooper]] accompanied [[Commander]] [[Pyre]] to the [[Trantor-class supertanker fuel depot|supertanker fuel depot]] ''[[Colossus]]'' on the [[planet]] [[Castilon]] to [[Hunt for Eila and Kel|hunt]] for two orphans from the planet [[Tehar]], [[Eila]] and [[Kel]].

They patrolled the [[Colossus marketplace|''Colossus'' marketplace]] before encountering Kel and chasing him to the [[Supertanker fuel depot|platform's]] [[Colossus Engineering Level|Engineering Level]], where they cornered the two [[Youngling|children]]. After the [[trooper]] and their companions were deceived into believing the orphans had [[Death|perished]], the [[First Order stormtrooper|stormtrooper]] left the ''Colossus'' to return to base.

==Biography==
{{Quote|There they are. Get them.|Pyre, to the tech stormtrooper|audio=PyreGetThem-TheChildrenFromTehar.mp3|<ref name="The Children from Tehar" />}}
[[File:HuntForKel-TheChildrenFromTehar.png|270px|thumb|left|Pyre orders the tech stormtooper to chase Kel.]]
In [[34 ABY]],<ref name="34 ABY">{{ResistanceDate|1|6}}</ref> a [[tech stormtrooper]] was dispatched to the [[Trantor-class supertanker fuel depot|refueling station]] ''[[Colossus]]''<ref name="The Children from Tehar" />&mdash;located on the [[planet]] [[Castilon]]<ref name="USWNE">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref>&mdash;after [[Captain]] [[Phasma]] received confirmation that two orphans&mdash;the only witnesses to the [[First Order]]'s [[Attack on Tehar|actions]] on<ref name="The Children from Tehar" /> the planet<ref name="USWNE" /> [[Tehar]]&mdash;had been spotted aboard the [[Supertanker fuel depot|station]]. They served under [[Commander]] [[Pyre]]'s [[Commanding officer|command]] alongside a standard [[Unidentified First Order stormtrooper (Colossus)|stormtrooper]]. The trio encountered an [[alien]] in the [[Colossus marketplace|''Colossus'' marketplace]], whom the tech [[First Order stormtrooper|stormtrooper]] interrogated with assistance from Pyre. Their colleague then spotted one of the [[Youngling|children]], [[Kel]], and the group gave [[Hunt for Eila and Kel|chase]] on Pyre's command.<ref name="The Children from Tehar" />

The child escaped into a chute with the help of [[Resistance]] [[spy]] [[Kazuda Xiono]] and his friends&mdash;the [[BB-series astromech droid|astromech droid]] [[BB-8]] and [[Technician|mechanic]] [[Neeku Vozo]]. After the group evaded the First Order, Pyre led the tech stormtrooper and his fellow [[trooper]] to the chute's exit, where they caught up with the fleeing targets. The First Order fired at the fleeing group with their [[F-11D blaster rifle|blasters]] set to [[stun]]. A locked door impeded the chase as the orphan's entourage escaped into the [[Colossus Engineering Level|Engineering Level]] of the ''Colossus''. Although the First Order group cut through the door, the escapees avoided the trooper's fire through another door with assistance from the [[Chelidae]] that lived in the ''Colossus''{{'s}} engineering.<ref name="The Children from Tehar" />

[[File:ScanningForChildren-TheChildrenFromTehar.png|255px|thumb|right|The tech stormtrooper scans the waters of Castilon for life signs.]]
After the First Order blasted through the next door, the trooper accompanied their entourage with their [[Blaster rifle|gun]] drawn as they approached a group of Chelidae protecting Kel and<ref name="The Children from Tehar" /> his<ref name="USWNE" /> [[Kel and Eila's family|sister]] [[Eila]]. Pyre then demanded the children come under First Order command or be [[Death|destroyed]], which the orphans refused and seemingly jumped into the [[water]]s of Castilon from an open grate. Under Pyre's instruction, the trooper scanned the water and reported slowing life signs and lowering body [[temperature]]s. The life signs were in reality those of the Chelidae masking themselves to deceive the First Order while the children safely hid below deck. Deceived into believing the children had perished and thereby satisfied, Pyre reported the success of the mission to Phasma and led the trooper and their companion back to base.<ref name="The Children from Tehar" />

==Personality and traits==
{{Quote|Life signs slowing. Body temperature dropping.|The tech stormtrooper, reporting information from their macro scope|audio=TechStormtrooper2-TheChildrenFromTehar.mp3|<ref name="The Children from Tehar" />}}
The tech stormtrooper was a [[human]]<ref name="Trooper" /> [[Gender|male]].<ref name="Topps" /> They followed Pyre's commands without hesitation and were calm as they reported the supposed deaths of Eila and Kel.<ref name="The Children from Tehar" />

==Equipment==
{{Quote|Scan the water for life signs.|Pyre, ordering the trooper to use their macro scope|audio=PyreSearchTheWater-TheChildrenFromTehar.mp3|<ref name="The Children from Tehar" />}}
The tech stormtrooper wore standard [[First Order stormtrooper armor]]. They carried a [[macro scope]] on their back and [[holster]]ed an F-11D [[blaster]] [[rifle]] on their right [[Limb|hip]]. The trooper utilized their [[Weapon|blaster's]] stun setting while pursuing Kel and their macro scope's scanning capability to confirm the orphans' supposed demise.<ref name="The Children from Tehar" />

==Behind the scenes==
The tech stormtrooper first appeared in "[[The Children from Tehar]],"<ref name="The Children from Tehar" /> the sixth episode of the [[Star Wars Resistance Season One|first season]] of the animated television series ''[[Star Wars Resistance]]'', which premiered on [[November 4]], [[2018]].<ref name="Disney Press">{{DisneyPress|wdtv=1|url=disneychannel/shows/star-wars-resistance/episodes|text=Star Wars Resistance}}</ref> They were credited as "Stormtrooper #1" and voiced by [[Lex Lang]].<ref name="The Children from Tehar" /> Prior to the episode's airing, the trooper appeared in the series' extended trailer earlier in the year on [[September 27]], which was posted on the official ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[Wikipedia:YouTube|YouTube]] channel.<ref name="Extended Trailer">{{SWYouTube|Ae2Cxy8sswk|Extended Sneak Peek &#124; Star Wars Resistance|sw_url=video/season-one-trailer-star-wars-resistance|date=2018-09-27}}</ref>

